    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43628" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐδίαιος</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῐαῖος</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hole in a ship</i>, for letting off the
			bilge-water, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.699f
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				1.92
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐδίαιον</span></b> , τό, <i>the end of a clyster-pipe</i>,
			Paul. ex Fest.<i><span class="en">
				p.69
			</span></i> L.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔδιον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Poll.
					4.181
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυναικεῖον μόριον</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρωκτός</span>
			, Id. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> as
				Adj., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐδιαῖος, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span></span>, <i>caught in fair weather</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριγόλας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sophr.
					67
				</span></i>
			.</div>
